; A rebuild that only replaces the SAT backend must not re-simplify the base.
;
; rebuildEncodings serves four purposes, and two of them -- retiring
; probe-based inprocessing and retiring trail reuse -- are configuration
; latches: the options can only be set on an empty solver, so the driver
; builds a fresh one and re-encodes into it. Nothing semantic has changed.
; The whole-base constant-bit, equality, simplification and unconstrained
; pass was welded to the rebuild rather than to its reason, so those latches
; paid for it too: measured at 18ms of a 3,001-conjunct base here, scaling
; with the base, for a rebuild whose entire purpose was to set one CaDiCaL
; option. Relief -- the rebuild that IS about size -- still runs it, which
; reencode-relief.smt2 pins.
;
; The floating-point conjunct retires trail reuse on the first solve; the
; base then stays fixed long enough for inprobing retirement to fire, and
; that rebuild must not mention re-simplifying anything.
; REQUIRES: floating-point
; RUN: %solver --incremental -s %s 2>&1 | %OutputCheck %s
; CHECK: inprobing retired
; CHECK-NOT: base re-simplified at rebuild
